# SABOTAGE: the grant personnel report resolves the HR name on the TENANT
# plane even when the mount is operator/impersonation.
#
# The report's whole masking watch-list guarantee is that the SAME projection
# asks `PiiResolution` with the ACTING scope. This patch replaces that scope
# with a tenant-plane mount, on the plausible reasoning that "the report is an
# internal compliance export, so it should show the names" — a change that
# still reads the grant org-scoped, still uses the opaque employee id, and
# still never touches a vault token, so every structural check stays green.
#
# Only the plane is gone. The operator DOM, CSV, and JSON now carry the clear
# name, which the red assertions in the report test MUST catch.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/grant_personnel_report_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: operator page is ••••, with no plaintext and no token
# MUST_FAIL: tenant CSV carries the clear name; operator CSV masks the SAME cell
# MUST_FAIL: tenant JSON carries the clear name; operator JSON masks the SAME row
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/grant_personnel.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/grant_personnel.ex
@@ -110,6 +110,6 @@
   defp resolved_report(mount, org_id, grant, config) do
     rows_mod = Mount.resource(mount, :GrantPersonnel)
-    scope = Mount.scope(mount, org_id)
+    scope = Mount.scope(%{mount | plane: Samen.Web.Plane.tenant()}, org_id)
 
     if Code.ensure_loaded?(rows_mod) do
       case GrantCompliance.personnel(grant, scope,
